      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Disciplinary hearing",
          "heading": "Tadhg Furlong faces disciplinary hearing today after Gavin Coombes citation",
          "body": "Tadhg Furlong faces a disciplinary committee today after being cited under Law 9.27 over Gavin Coombes' allegation that his groin was interfered with in the Leinster-Munster URC game. Leinster assistant Robin McBryde has defended the prop, saying \"He's got no history of anything like that.\" Owen Doyle, a former head of Irish referees, argues any guilty verdict should be heavy enough to rule Furlong out of Ireland's November Tests, pointing to nine weeks for Jan-Hendrik Wessels in a similar case."
        },
