    "467": {
      "date": "2026-10-29",
      "edition": "Thursday 29 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Record chase",
          "heading": "Markus Muller's Test debut would make him youngest Springbok in professional era",
          "body": "Markus Muller is poised to break a Springboks record if he makes his debut in the Nations Championship matches against Italy, France or Ireland. Planet Rugby reports he would become the youngest Springbok of the professional era, displacing Frans Steyn, who debuted at 19 years, 181 days under Jake White. Muller, who only turned 19 in July, started the key fixtures at the U20 World Championship and scored in the final win over France."
        },
